**Definition 11.1 (the still-open all-size obligation).** At each
$d\ge1$, the original target remains a total computable predicate
$V(d,\mu,C,\pi)$ on rational probabilities, positive rational caps
and finite strings, such that acceptance implies

$$
\forall n\ge1\ \forall\Theta,\qquad
\sum_{x\in C_\Theta}\prod_i\mu(x_i)\le C^n,
\tag{GDB.47}
$$

and such that for every rational $\epsilon>0$ some accepted label
satisfies $-\log_2C>\sigma_d-\epsilon$. The alternative sufficient
bridge is a uniform effective length error

$$
\sigma_d\ge\frac{\log_2K_d(n)}n-\eta_d(n),\qquad
\eta_d(n)\longrightarrow0,
\tag{GDB.48}
$$

with effective control sufficient for terminating two-sided approximation
of the same original $\lambda$. These are the unresolved [NPC, §8][NPC]
and [SIR, §9][SIR] obligations. Exact finite evaluation, a finite alphabet,
proof enumeration and semantic compactness do not close them.

Theorem 3.2 permits exact forced-phase elimination with all original
